Subject: [PATCH] PhoneWindowManager: a controller button can run a PocketDS Extra macro

A button remapped to a macro sends the key code 1000 + the macro number (1001 to 1099, set by the
input reader from persist.sys.pocketds.keymap). The system takes it before any app (the key down
and up never reach a window) and, on the key down, tells PocketDS Extra which macro to play with
the broadcast org.lineageos.pocketds.parts.MACRO (extra "id"). PocketDS Extra presses the keys of
the macro itself (Macros.java).

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -4800,6 +4800,7 @@
     private static final int POCKETDS_KEY_HOME = KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_7;      // violet
     private static final int POCKETDS_KEY_PROFILE = KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_8;   // green
     private static final long POCKETDS_LONG_PRESS_MS = 600;
+    private static final int POCKETDS_MACRO_BASE = 1000;
 
     /**
      * The extra buttons of the console ("AYANEO DEVICE" and the central button of "AYANEO
@@ -4816,6 +4817,18 @@
             return false;
         }
         final int code = event.getKeyCode();
+        // A button of the controller set to run a macro sends the key code 1000 + the macro
+        // number (1001...1099, no real key has them): the apps never see it, PocketDS Extra plays
+        // the macro when the button goes down.
+        if (code > POCKETDS_MACRO_BASE && code <= POCKETDS_MACRO_BASE + 99) {
+            if (event.getAction() == KeyEvent.ACTION_DOWN && event.getRepeatCount() == 0) {
+                final int id = code - POCKETDS_MACRO_BASE;
+                mHandler.post(() -> mContext.sendBroadcastAsUser(
+                        new Intent("org.lineageos.pocketds.parts.MACRO").putExtra("id", id)
+                                .setPackage(POCKETDS_PACKAGE), UserHandle.CURRENT));
+            }
+            return true;
+        }
         if (code != POCKETDS_KEY_SWAP && code != POCKETDS_KEY_OVERLAY
                 && code != POCKETDS_KEY_HOME && code != POCKETDS_KEY_PROFILE
                 && code != KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_MODE) {
